/**
 * @file fflags_test.cpp
 * @brief fflags the RISC-V way, on all five models (known_issues 72, 116).
 *
 * RISC-V's fflags: NX bit 0, UF 1, OF 2, DZ 3, NV 4. An FP op ORs the flags
 * it raises into fflags; nothing clears them but a CSR write. Double ops
 * report every flag, not a bool. Loads, stores, moves, sign injection and
 * fclass raise nothing (116: they used to clear the flags).
 *
 * Per-op programs clear fflags before each op and store it right after, so
 * every stored word is exactly what that op raised: rounding in rne/rtz/
 * rdn/rup (rmm only off ties, 113), exact and inexact results, overflow,
 * underflow into subnormals (tininess after rounding), zeros, infinities,
 * quiet and signaling NaNs. "Accrual" ORs several ops into one read, keeps
 * 31 across exact ops, and keeps DZ across fsw/flw/fsd/fld.
 *
 * Every expected word comes from ~/atlas-verify/e5/gen_fflags.py and its
 * oracle fpo.py (exact Fraction arithmetic and the IEEE / RISC-V special
 * cases), never from a model. The programs are stored unpadded and padded
 * here, four nops after every instruction, so all five models owe them.
 */
